{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"MatomoEncoding"}],"title":"MatomoEncoding","externalID":"MatomoEncoding","symbolKind":"module"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Sending to Matomo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoSetupError"],"anchor":"Sending-to-Matomo"},{"title":"Custom dimensions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions","doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoUnmappedProperty"],"anchor":"Custom-dimensions"},{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") for one site of a Matomo installation in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one call. It checks the installation’s URL, the site ID, the category and the custom dimensions,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then posts bulk tracking requests to the installation’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"matomo.php"},{"text":" with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". Each batch is split to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": 20 records a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request, as Matomo’s iOS SDK sends them, and 1,000,000 bytes a request, under the 1 MiB that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nginx takes in a body by default, as Matomo documents no limit. A batch with no record the encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can write, an empty one included, makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves this module out, so import it on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo takes events from anyone who can reach it, so the destination needs no key, and builds on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every platform: an app sends to Matomo directly."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MatomoEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let matomo = try HTTPDestination.matomo(","    url: url,  \/\/ where Matomo is installed: https:\/\/analytics.example.com","    siteID: 3,  \/\/ the app's site in Matomo","    dimensions: [\"plan\": 1],  \/\/ custom dimensions made in Matomo","    category: \"Shop\",  \/\/ each event's category","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: matomo)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"url"},{"text":" is where Matomo is installed, with its path if it has one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/example.com\/matomo\/"},{"text":"), not the tracker’s endpoint: the destination appends ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"matomo.php"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"itself. The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoSetupError"},{"text":" for a URL that isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"text":", has no host, holds a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"user name, password, query or fragment, or already ends in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".php"},{"text":" file such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"matomo.php"},{"text":"; for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a site ID below 1; for a category that is empty once trimmed, or longer than the 4,096 characters","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Matomo stores; and for dimensions that break a rule, listed below.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"No token_auth","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"No-tokenauth"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination sends no "},{"code":"token_auth","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and takes none. A token is a secret, and anything an app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ships can be read out of it, so a token in an app gives anyone who has the app the token’s rights"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over your Matomo."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without a token, Matomo takes an event’s time ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cdt"},{"type":"text","text":") only when it is less than a day old, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses one more than a day ahead. It answers 200 to such a request all the same, and stores"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing, so the encoder leaves out every record tracked more than 23 hours before or after it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encodes the batch, and the destination reports it, the hour to spare for a queue on the server and clocks that disagree. So a record that waits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more than 23 hours to be encoded, kept by a store through a long time offline or waiting in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"buffer behind a failing delivery, is reported as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError\/timestampOutsideWindow","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and never reaches Matomo."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request is encoded once, and each retry sends the same bytes, so the encoder gives each request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a deadline 23 hours after its oldest record was tracked. A request still failing by then isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent again, as it would reach Matomo too late to be stored: the destination drops the whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request, its younger records too, and reports it on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":", with every one of its records’ identifiers. Only the past side of the window needs a deadline: a retry arrives later, never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"earlier, so it can’t carry a record further ahead of Matomo’s clock than it was. The window is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured with the device’s clock, which Matomo can’t see: a device whose clock is wrong by more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than a day has every record refused, without an error. A clock that reads NaN or infinite has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every record left out and reported."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To keep older records, send them to a server you run, such as a TraffluentCollector, and have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that server forward them to Matomo with a token of a user who has write access to the site,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"added as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token_auth"},{"type":"text","text":" to its bulk request’s JSON. A token on a server stays secret. This module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doesn’t do that."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Visitors are sessions","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Visitors-are-sessions"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo counts a visitor per ","type":"text"},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", 16 hexadecimal digits. The destination sends the last 64 bits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the record’s session, from the sessions enricher, in lowercase hex. Nothing else identifies a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record: no ","type":"text"},{"code":"uid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"cid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", device identifier or account. So Matomo’s visitors are sessions, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its returning-visitor and visits-per-visitor reports say how long sessions last, not whether","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"people come back. That is the library’s default, for privacy. Each session is one visit as long","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the sessions enricher’s timeout is no longer than Matomo’s visit length, 30 minutes by default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"visit_standard_length","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). With a longer timeout, a session that pauses for longer than Matomo’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"visit length becomes two visits of one visitor.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A record with no session, such as one a store recovered after a relaunch, is its own visitor: its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the last 64 bits of the record’s identifier. Making up a session would join unrelated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records, and skipping the record would lose it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo recognizes a visitor by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and, failing that, by a fingerprint of the request’s IP"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"address, User-Agent, language and a daily salt, within 30 minutes. A new session’s first event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":" Matomo hasn’t seen, so Matomo may fold it into another visit from the same address"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and User-Agent: an earlier session on the same device, or a session of another person behind the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same network. Set "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trust_visitors_cookies = 1"},{"type":"text","text":" under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Tracker]"},{"type":"text","text":" in Matomo’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"config.ini.php"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have Matomo match a request that has an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":" by its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":" alone, for every site of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"installation. When Matomo’s privacy setting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to force tracking without cookies is on, Matomo ignores "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"},{"type":"text","text":", and every visit is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fingerprint’s."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo records the address each request comes from, as no app can override it without a token.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It masks part of the address before storing it when “Anonymize Visitors’ IP addresses” is on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Administration, Privacy, Anonymize data). In Matomo 5.14 and 6.0 it is on, masking 2 bytes, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an installation whose administrator has never changed it, so a fresh install has it on, and an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"older one keeps the setting it had. Matomo still uses the full address for geolocation and for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the fingerprint above unless “Also use the Anonymized IP addresses when enriching visits” is on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"too, which is off by default. Check both settings before you send.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What Matomo receives","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"What-Matomo-receives"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a JSON object, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"requests\":[…]}"},{"text":", holding one tracking request per record, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"?"},{"text":" and a query string, every value percent-encoded but for letters, digits, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"."},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"~"},{"text":". Each tracking request is a Matomo event:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"idsite"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The site ID","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rec"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"apiv"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session’s last 64 bits, or the record’s"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"cdt","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s time, in whole seconds since 1970","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ca"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so Matomo doesn’t take the request for a page view should its Events plugin be off"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"e_c","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The category you give, such as your app’s name"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"e_a"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s name"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lang"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s locale, as a BCP 47 identifier, when it has ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"dimension<ID>","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The value of each property the dimensions map","type":"text"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo’s Events reports group events by category, then action, then name. The category is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"argument you give, as an app’s events have no grouping Matomo would show better, and the action is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the event’s name, so the Event Actions report lists your events. No event name (","type":"text"},{"code":"e_n","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") or value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"e_v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") is sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The User-Agent is the one ","type":"text"},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends, which Matomo reads for the device and operating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system. The rest of the standard context isn’t sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Custom dimensions","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Custom-dimensions"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo numbers each site’s custom dimensions as you make them (Administration, Websites, Custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Dimensions), so "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions"},{"type":"text","text":" maps your plan’s property names to their IDs:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[\"plan\": 1, \"seats\": 2]"},{"type":"text","text":". A property is mapped by name in every event that has it. Its value is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":": a string as it is, a number as JSON writes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, a Boolean as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", and an array or object as its JSON. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" sends no value."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" property is never sent, whatever the record reveals, so it can’t be mapped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A property no dimension is mapped to is never sent, and the record goes without it. When the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination is made, it logs a notice for each event with such properties, once."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoDimensions\/unmappedProperties(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them, so a test can check that every property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you mean to send has a dimension."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The factory throws for a dimension ID below 1, a property mapped twice, a property no event of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan has, a property that is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" in an event, and two properties of one event mapped to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one dimension, checked in that order."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make each dimension in Matomo with the Action scope, so each event keeps its own value. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension of the Visit scope holds one value a visit, the last one sent. Matomo ignores a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension it has no dimension of that ID for, and stores at most 250 characters of a value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Records left out","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write, or that Matomo would refuse or change, is left out and the rest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the batch is sent:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name is empty once Matomo removes line breaks and trims it, or longer than the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"4,096 characters Matomo stores of an action;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose timestamp has no whole seconds of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or is more than 23 hours from when the batch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is encoded;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a dimension’s value longer than 250 characters;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose tracking request is more than a request of 1,000,000 bytes can hold."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lengths are counted as Matomo stores the text: without line breaks or NUL characters, trimmed of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spaces and tabs at either end, and with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"&"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":">"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\""},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"'"},{"type":"text","text":" written as the HTML entities"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Matomo stores them as, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"&"},{"type":"text","text":" counts 5. Matomo removes the line breaks and trims the spaces of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name or value it keeps too."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding\/MatomoEncodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event of the plan"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose name would be left out."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"What Matomo doesn’t report","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"What-Matomo-doesnt-report"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Matomo answers 200 to a bulk request it can read, whatever its tracking requests hold. One it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses is counted as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invalid"},{"type":"text","text":" in the answer’s JSON and not stored, and only a request with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"token learns which. So a wrong site ID, a site that doesn’t exist, and events of a time Matomo"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses are lost without an error. Check that the first events show up in the site’s Visits Log."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A server set to require a token for every bulk request ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bulk_requests_require_authentication"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses each one: Matomo 6.0 answers 400, which the destination drops and reports, and Matomo 5.14"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answers 500, which the destination retries until the request is cancelled. Leave that setting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"off."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Matomo doesn’t remove duplicates. A record is sent more than once when a request is retried after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Matomo stored it but the answer was lost, when a delivery sends a cancelled batch again, and when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a store redelivers records after a relaunch, and Matomo counts each copy.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Matomo receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/matomoencoding"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Matomo installation as events, through its bulk tracking API."}],"references":{"doc://MatomoEncoding/documentation/MatomoEncoding":{"title":"MatomoEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/matomoencoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatomoEncoding\/documentation\/MatomoEncoding","role":"collection","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Matomo installation as events, through its bulk tracking API."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://MatomoEncoding/documentation/MatomoEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the site ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"siteID"},{"text":" of the Matomo installation at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"url"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each event in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"category"},{"text":" and each property ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dimensions"},{"text":" maps as its custom dimension,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"text":" on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/matomoencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/matomo(url:siteid:dimensions:category:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"matomo"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"url"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"siteID"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"dimensions"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatomoEncoding0A10DimensionsV","text":"MatomoDim